# a) Push the function/constant token
# b) Re-tokenize the remaining chars by adjusting the position

# But `i` has already been advanced past "e2pi"!
# I need to backtrack `i` to account for the remaining chars.

# The fix: instead of just advancing past all alphanumeric chars at once,
# I should advance only past the MATCHED function/constant name.

# For "e2pi": read "e2pi" (5 chars: e,2,p,i), match "e" (1 char)
# After matching "e", we should set i = start + "e".len() = start + 1
# So the remaining "2pi" gets processed in subsequent iterations!

